{
  "_comment": "wiki related weights a shared hook by IDF with a stopword floor at the dilution threshold (12). A hook shared via a rare hook (df 2) is a strong bridge; a hook on >12 cards contributes 0. Here tgt shares 'rare-hook' with rare-mate only (df 2 -> weight 2*ln(12/2)=3.58) and 'over-applied-hook' with 13 dh-* cards (df 14 -> weight 0). All cards share tag 'idea' (+2). So rare-mate scores 2+3.58=5.6 while each dh-* scores tag-only 2.0 (the diluted hook adds nothing). Locks the IDF floor: spurious over-applied hooks cannot manufacture bridges.",
  "setup": [
